          <baseCommit>7ffd941d69cb5bcb727a06426f32dba77b8cac6f</baseCommit>
          <output>All 13 warnings and 5 errors are pre-existing, in unrelated frozen `_meta/transform` history files and other sectors — none touch the 35 rendered A04 pages. All changes are scoped exactly to `a04_rendering/data/page/docs/*.bml` (35 files), nothing else was touched, and nothing was committed.

The A04_02_RenderPages task is complete:

- **35/35 A04 DocPages rendered** — semantic scaffold (purpose/message/role/weight/detailLevel/authoritativeSources/etc.) replaced with finished reader-facing prose in the same `content` tree, then all scaffold metadata stripped, keeping `title`/`detailLevel`/`pageType`/`content`/`references`.
- **Sourcing**: every claim traces to the page's bound `org.blockml.bml.documentation.*` / `core.*` / `definition.*` / `type.*` Block(s), resolved via `blockml inspect`, falling back to reading the dependency `.bml` directly when `inspect` truncated long documentation. No a01/a02/a03 content or cross-sector FQNs leaked in.
- **Process**: I rendered TableOfContents, Introduction, and CoreUseCases myself to lock in the pattern, then split the remaining 32 pages across 8 parallel agents by page group (Foundations, Type System, Members, Behaviour &amp; Values + BML Format, Composition &amp; Structure).
- **Validation**: `npx blockml validate --all` — 719 blocks, 5 errors / 13 warnings, all pre-existing and confined to frozen historical `_meta/transform` records and an unrelated `a03_authoring` example file. Zero errors, warnings, or gaps reported against any of the 35 rendered pages.
- **No gaps** — every page's scaffold had enough `message`/`supportingPoints` plus a resolvable authoritative source to render responsibly.

I did not commit and did not touch the running transform record (`_meta/transform/running/T00013_BuildA04_20260917T012756.bml`) — flipping the &quot;Render A04 pages&quot; operation to Succeeded and committing is a separate step, same as the prior A04 build.</output>
